From 325788575df6c1ef937985ad43d63169d6d9eaab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Palinar <marco@street63.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:06:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Flush stdout after each REPL command so a pipe-driven session
 parses live

linenoise already reads plain lines when stdin is not a TTY, which makes
the REPL a daemon any script can drive over a pipe -- except that libc
block-buffers stdout on pipes, so the "Done -> <path> [Xs]" completion
markers could sit unseen until the process exited. One flush at the end
of each loop iteration makes every confirmation and completion line
observable as it happens. TacticaArena's roll.mjs --seeds mode relies on
this to post-process each clip while the next seed is still generating.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012n1R74RWBtL3Qos3GyyBRx
---
 h3_cli.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/h3_cli.c b/h3_cli.c
index 2bb6c8b..4aec192 100644
--- a/h3_cli.c
+++ b/h3_cli.c
@@ -827,6 +827,10 @@ int h3_cli_run(h3_ctx *ctx, const char *model_dir,
             }
             else if (*input != '!') generate(&state, input);
         }
+        /* A daemon driving this loop over a pipe (linenoise's no-TTY path)
+         * parses stdout live; libc block-buffers pipes, so without a flush
+         * the "Done -> ..." line can sit unseen until the process exits. */
+        fflush(stdout);
         free(line);
     }
     if (*history) linenoiseHistorySave(history);
